    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature: a request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner response returns `salutation = title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nFollowing the project's OpenAPI-generated-DTO + MapStruct + OfficeFloor architecture, the change threads a stored `title` through create \u2192 persist \u2192 read:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` string property to the `OwnerFields` (request) schema and a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` (response) schema. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`) are generated from this spec at build time.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, so the value survives `POST` \u2192 `GET`.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", ...)` backed by a `toSalutation(owner)` helper implementing the compose rule. `title` maps automatically by name in both directions.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a nullable `title` column to the `owners` table (the test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in schema.sql). Existing `data.sql` inserts use explicit column lists, so they're unaffected.\n\nThe pipeline already publishes the request body as `OwnerFieldsDto`, builds the entity via `OwnerMapper.toOwner`, saves it, and responds via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` \u2014 so no YAML/function wiring changes were needed.\n\nTests: the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
